From: Joan Karadimov <joan.karadimov@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Resolve MSYS2 paths against the root this tool is installed in

octopi is a native program managing an MSYS2 installation, so the paths it
shares with libalpm are not paths it can open itself: MSYS2's / is a
directory on a Windows drive. libalpm's side of this is handled -- alpmrpc's
client takes and returns Win32 paths, converted on the server -- but the
files octopi reads on its own account never go near libalpm, and those are
what this is for: /usr/bin/checkupdates, /etc/pacman.conf, and the MSYS2
programs it runs.

The root is found the way alpmrpc's client finds its server: positionally,
from where this executable is, since the tool is installed at
<root>/<env>/bin. GetModuleFileNameW rather than QCoreApplication, because
the startup checks that need it run before the QApplication object exists.

msysPath() is deliberately not a general translator, and the comment on it
says so: /bin is a mount alias for /usr/bin and /c is C:, and neither
survives being prefixed. Converting those needs Cygwin's mount table, which
lives in msys-2.0.dll -- the one library this process must never load.
Nothing octopi opens itself is one of those.

Note what is left alone: the four other mentions of /etc/pacman.conf in
package.cpp sit inside a shell command string, run by a shell that wants
POSIX, so translating them would break them.

Not for upstream: meaningless where / is /.
diff --git a/notifier/main.cpp b/notifier/main.cpp
index 63c5ed6..61e08cb 100644
